To start your DAG after system restart, do only these steps. ✅

# 1. SSH into VM

Open terminal.

---

# 2. Activate Airflow Environment

Run:

```bash id="d8y2qf"
source ~/airflow-env/bin/activate
```

---

# 3. Start Airflow

Run:

```bash id="p4n7tx"
airflow standalone
```

Keep this terminal OPEN.

---

# 4. Open Airflow UI

Open browser:

```text id="x6r1mv"
http://136.116.97.149:8080
```

---

# 5. Login

Username:

```text id="n9w4zk"
admin
```

Password:
shown in terminal where `airflow standalone` started.

---

# 6. Turn DAG ON

Find DAG:

```text id="r2v8jy"
realtime_pipeline_monitoring
```

Enable toggle if OFF.

---

# 7. Trigger DAG

Click:

```text id="j5m3cx"
▶ Trigger DAG
```

Now DAG starts automatically:

* Zookeeper
* Kafka
* Generator
* Enricher
* Beam pipeline

---

# 8. Verify DAG Running

In Airflow UI:

* tasks should turn GREEN

---

# 9. Verify BigQuery

Run:

```sql id="c3p7vr"
SELECT
COUNT(*) AS total_rows,
MAX(processing_time) AS latest_time
FROM `project-6e64a1a1-8e69-4a88-93d.realtime_analytics.streaming_metrics`;
```

If:

* rows increase
* latest_time updates

then your DAG and full pipeline are working correctly.
